    "extraction_output_tokens": 256,
    "extraction_prompt": "Extract compact, source-grounded facts from the CURRENT event for workflow memory.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object, no prose or Markdown:\n{\"evidence\":[{\"source_refs\":[\"CURRENT_EVENT_ID\"],\"subject_ref\":\"agent\",\"predicate\":\"action\",\"value\":\"short action description\",\"event_kind\":\"attempt\"}]}\n\nThe entire response must fit within 220 output tokens. Return at most TWO\nconcise items. Only the five fields in the example are required; omit all\noptional bookkeeping fields (IDs, source_versions, revision, modality,\ncertainty and source_spans). The builder supplies those fields. Keep each\nvalue short, preferably below 80 characters. Do not copy complete actions,\nmessages, URLs or accessibility trees if they are long; describe the fact\nconcisely, preserving important names, numbers and dates. Close all JSON.\n\nRecord the current action as an `attempt`, even when no success was observed.\nIf pre_state or post_state supports a useful visible fact, add one\n`observation` (for example page title, selected field, address or date).\nAn explicit observed_outcome may be a `confirmation` or `failure`. Actions,\ngoals, plans and messages alone do NOT establish successful state changes.\nAn answer sent to a user is a reported claim, not verified UI state.\n\nUse prefix context only to resolve references; extract facts of the current\nevent, not previous events again. Every source_refs must contain only the\ncurrent event_id from the input. Keep subjects local to its scope. Valid\nevent_kind values: intent, attempt, observation, confirmation, failure.\nReturn an empty evidence list only when the current event contains no action,\ngoal, pre_state, post_state or observed_outcome. Never invent missing facts.",
